  m_Name: Object_39
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Left Rear Bolt (2)
  description: The Left Rear Bolt (2) is a tiny, complex-shaped component situated
    at the top-left-rear of the engine, constructed from Material.001, responsible
    for fastening the rear section of the engine, thereby maintaining its structural
    integrity and preventing potential damage from stress and strain, and its compact
    design enables it to fit snugly in tight spaces. This bolt works in conjunction
    with other bolts to distribute the engine's weight evenly. The rear position
    of the bolt also subjects it to varying levels of stress due to the engine's
    operation.
